help_intro = One player holds the phone to their forehead, screen facing out, without peeking. Everyone else gives clues until that player guesses the word on the screen.
help_play = How to play
help_play_1 = • Pick a deck, then put the phone on your forehead. The round starts when you hold it steady.
help_play_2 = • **Nod** to tilt the phone down when you guess right. **Tip your head back** to tilt it up and pass.
help_play_3 = • Clue-givers can describe, act out or hum the word, but can't say it, spell it or point at it.
help_play_4 = • When time runs out, see which words you got and which you passed. A deck doesn't repeat a word until you've played through all of them.
help_buttons = Without tilting
help_buttons_1 = • On a device with no motion sensor, or with **Answer by Tilting** off in Settings, use the **Correct** and **Pass** buttons. On a keyboard, press ↓ or Return for correct and ↑ to pass.
